  "provider_query": "Public Telegram web preview of the official Telegram channel",
  "answer": "The official Telegram channel is **@telegram** (“Telegram News”). Its public web preview is available without an account.\n\n1. **Channel preview (latest posts)** — https://t.me/s/telegram  \n   Official description: “The official Telegram on Telegram.” Subscriber counts on the preview have been reported around 9–11.5M. [web:8] [web:12]\n\n2. **Channel join / view page** — https://t.me/telegram  \n   Standard public link; browsers often offer “Preview channel” before opening the app. [web:8]\n\n3. **Example older post in the preview** — https://t.me/s/telegram/81  \n   Same channel rendered as HTML (text, views, media prompts). [web:12]\n\n4. **Paging older posts** — https://t.me/s/telegram?before=461  \n   Public preview supports `?before=<post-id>` to step backward through recent history. [web:8] [web:2]\n\n5. **How the preview works** — Public channels use `https://t.me/s/<username>`. It returns roughly the last ~20 posts as HTML (text, view counts, timestamps, some media). No login or bot token required. [web:1] [web:2] [web:3]\n\n6. **Embed public posts** — https://core.telegram.org/widgets/post  \n   Official docs: open a public `t.me` post link and use the embed option. [web:7]\n\n7. **Third-party browser layer** — https://tg.me/  \n   Unofficial site that opens public `t.me` links in the browser (e.g. `t.me/name` → `tg.me/name`) with extra stats. Not operated by Telegram. [web:0]\n\n8. **Another public viewer** — https://anonytg.com/public-telegram-channel-viewer/  \n   Third-party viewer for supported public channels and posts, with links back to Telegram. [web:4]\n\n**Note:** Telegram says official announcements are only on telegram.org and this channel; other “official” sites are often scams. [web:12]",
